    { question: "What are Hall Effect analog sticks and why are they immune to drift?", answer: "Hall Effect sensors use magnetic sensors instead of physical contacts, completely eliminating mechanical contact wear." },
    { question: "How do I fix analog stick drift on my controller?", answer: "Fixes include cleaning potentiometers with 99% isopropyl alcohol, adjusting in-game dead-zones, or installing Hall Effect replacement modules." },
    { question: "What is a dead-zone setting in games like CS2, Call of Duty, and Fortnite?", answer: "Dead-zone settings create an inner threshold circle ignoring small stick movements, preventing subtle drift from affecting gameplay." },
    { question: "Can I test both Left and Right analog sticks simultaneously?", answer: "Yes, dual polar plots track both Left (Axes 0/1) and Right (Axes 2/3) stick boundaries." },
